---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import shelfData from '../data/shelf.json';

const allPosts = await getCollection('blog', ({ data }) => data.status === 'live');
const reviewCount = allPosts.filter(p => p.data.postType === 'review').length;
const totalBooksRead = shelfData.length;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title="About — Saturdays in a Book" description="Sabtain Khan, reading in Brooklyn. Reviews, lists, and recommendations." />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main class="about-page">

			<!-- Hero -->
			<div class="about-hero">
				<div class="bleed">
					<div class="avatar-side">
						<div class="avatar-wrap">
							<img src="/sk-notion-face.png" alt="Sabtain Khan" />
						</div>
					</div>
					<div class="bio-side">
						<p class="crumbs">§ About Me</p>
						<h1>Hi, I'm <em>Sabtain.</em></h1>
						<p class="lede">
							I live in Brooklyn and love to read books, then talk about them with
							anyone who'll sit still long enough to listen to me ramble on.
						</p>
						<div class="sig-strip">
							<span><strong>{reviewCount}</strong> reviews · <strong>{totalBooksRead}</strong> books read</span>
							<span>Brooklyn, NY</span>
							<a href="https://www.goodreads.com/saturdays" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Goodreads ↗</a>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- Body -->
			<div class="about-body">
				<div class="measure">
					<article>
						<p class="intro">
							There was a point in my life, around 2014, where I decided to get into the habit of reading. Since then, I've read hundreds of books. A lot of my friends, colleagues, and strangers I meet love to ask me about books I've read and recommendations. I thought it would be nice to leave my notes and thoughts and more here for them. A place to discover more about my journey, hopefully helping you find your next book to read.
						</p>
						<h2>How I rate</h2>
						<div class="rating-section">
							<div class="rating-key">
								<div class="rk-stars">★☆☆☆☆</div>
								<div class="rk-row">
									<strong>Don't recommend</strong>
									Derivative or dishonest, or just plain bad writing. Don't waste your time.
								</div>

								<div class="rk-stars">★★☆☆☆</div>
								<div class="rk-row">
									<strong>Readable, but offers little</strong>
									Low literary value; mostly forgettable.
								</div>

								<div class="rk-stars">★★★☆☆</div>
								<div class="rk-row">
									<strong>Recommended, with caveats</strong>
									I enjoyed it, but I won't push it on you.
								</div>

								<div class="rk-stars">★★★★☆</div>
								<div class="rk-row">
									<strong>Really recommend</strong>
									I'd go out of my way to suggest it.
								</div>

								<div class="rk-stars">★★★★★</div>
								<div class="rk-row">
									<strong>Recommend to almost everyone</strong>
									Fundamentally different. Timeless.
								</div>
							</div>

							<div class="scoring-callout">
								<div class="lbl">A note on scoring</div>
								<p>I hate scoring systems at times, so here's a rubric for how I think about it.</p>
								<p>A 5/5 book should mean 100/100, and 4/5 means 80/100. I take that quite seriously, and the space between that can be brutal. So when I read something that feels like a 90/100, I round <em>down</em>, not up, to a 4/5.</p>
								<p>The scale doesn't capture the nuance I wish it could, and I blame scoring systems like Goodreads which only allow whole-star ratings. Overall I still see myself as lenient.</p>
							</div>
						</div>

						<h2>How I review</h2>
						<p>
							All of my reviews are genuinely mine. I try to avoid summarizing the entire book, and rather capture what interests me. Some books I have a particularly bigger interest in and I can get carried away with writing a little more about it.
						</p>
						<p>I have a backlog of reviews, so you can see my entire shelf of books I've read, or filter that down to just the books I've reviewed.</p>
						<div class="about-ctas">
							<a href="/book-reviews" class="hero-cta">Browse all reviews →</a>
							<a href="/book-reviews?status=all" class="hero-cta">Browse entire shelf →</a>
						</div>
					</article>
				</div>
			</div>

		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
/* Avatar left on desktop/tablet */
.avatar-side { order: 1; }
.bio-side    { order: 2; }
</style>
